6. Security recommendation

One thing I want to emphasize: Excel worksheet protection is mainly an editing restriction, not strong security.

For your requirement:

> "The WinActor output Excel can't be edited by someone."



I would use two layers:

WinActor
                ↓
         Generate .xls
                ↓
      VBA Worksheet Protection
                ↓
       Windows Folder Permission
                ↓
          User can READ
          User cannot MODIFY

The VBA protection prevents normal editing inside Excel.

Windows folder permissions can prevent the user from simply replacing or overwriting the original file.

If the requirement is simply "users should not accidentally change the WinActor output"

VBA worksheet protection is a good solution.

If the requirement is "users must absolutely not be able to modify the original file"

Use Windows/SharePoint permissions in addition to VBA protection.


