43. Concurrency

There are actually two separate concurrency issues:

Excel overwrite

Solved by unique filenames:

Request ID + Timestamp

Duplicate processing

Solved by:

ProcessingStatus

or a request/header record.

Power Automate also provides trigger concurrency control. By default, trigger concurrency is off; Microsoft documents enabling it when you need to control simultaneous runs. 

For your design, I would not rely on concurrency control as the main protection. Unique filenames are better because different requests should be allowed to run at the same time.


