44. Another Important Excel Best Practice

Your Office Script should use:

workbook.getWorksheet("Reactivation Form 2")

instead of:

workbook.getActiveWorksheet()

because Power Automate runs Office Scripts in an independent Excel session and there may be no meaningful "active" worksheet. Microsoft specifically recommends avoiding relative references such as getActiveWorksheet() in Power Automate scripts. 

Your script above already follows this best practice.


