45. Date Handling

Power Automate uses UTC, while Excel doesn't have a fixed inherent timezone. If the dates in your SharePoint list are date/time columns, make sure you format them deliberately before sending them to the script. Microsoft documents this Power Automate/Excel timezone difference. 

For example:

formatDateTime(
    triggerBody()?['RequestDate'],
    'MM/dd/yyyy'
)

and:

formatDateTime(
    triggerBody()?['ReactivationDate'],
    'MM/dd/yyyy'
)

If you only need the date, this is preferable to passing the raw ISO timestamp.


